  "description": "Glory sets two tepee towers apart and joins them with a rope net bridge. Red slides run off both towers, one of them a tube slide, and a climbing wall gives a harder way up. Children cross the bridge back and forth, so the structure works best for groups who like to explore. It takes 40 to 45 children. At 46'5\" by 25'2\", with a safe play area of 52'5\" x 31'2\", Glory is long rather than wide. It suits a strip along a park boundary or the side of a school ground. Listed skills are exploring, confidence, creative thinking and strength. It comes in mixed colours. Our 3-year warranty applies to the galvanised pipe, moulded slides, composite laminates and rope bridge. Send us your site dimensions and we will draw it in.",
